<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1953 CE – present · capital Cairo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Modern republican Egypt, founded after the 1952 revolution, a leading Arab state under Nasser, Sadat, Mubarak and their successors.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Free Officers overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farouk-of-egypt">King Farouk</a> in 1952, they abolished the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-egypt">Kingdom of Egypt</a> on 18 June 1953, proclaiming a republic with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-naguib">Muhammad Naguib</a> as president. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Gamal Abdel Nasser</a> sidelined Naguib in 1954 and became president in 1956.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Nasser</a> nationalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> in 1956, surviving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Anglo-French-Israeli invasion</a>, built the Aswan High Dam and pursued Arab socialism and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pan-arabism">pan-Arabism</a>, merging with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-arab-republic">United Arab Republic</a> from 1958 to 1961. After defeat in 1967, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> fought the 1973 war and made peace with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> in 1979. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hosni-mubarak">Hosni Mubarak</a> ruled from 1981 for three decades.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hosni-mubarak">Mubarak</a> fell in the 2011 uprising. The elected president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-morsi">Mohamed Morsi</a> was removed by the army in 2013, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdel-fattah-el-sisi">Abdel Fattah el-Sisi</a> has ruled since 2014. The Arab Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> remains the most populous Arab state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Republic of Egypt" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Egypt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1953 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cairo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gamal Abdel Nasser, Anwar Sadat, Hosni Mubarak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam; Coptic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arab Republic of Egypt, Egypt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1990&amp;focus=republic-of-egypt" aria-label="Republic of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5491 1081 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5811 1337L5811 1337M5811 1337L5811 1337"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5811 1337h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cairo. <a href="/atlas?year=1990&amp;focus=republic-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
